{"seq":3,"slug":"the-warring-states-era","title":"The Warring States Era","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/life-and-times/the-warring-states-era","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"an-age-of-chaos","title":"乱世的背景","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/life-and-times/the-warring-states-era/an-age-of-chaos","wordCount":1841,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"laozi-and-the-daoist-stream","title":"老子与道家","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/zhuangzi/life-and-times/the-warring-states-era/laozi-and-the-daoist-stream","wordCount":1746,"readingTime":7}],"introMarkdown":"本章呈现庄子所处的乱世背景及其道家渊源。庄子生活在战乱频仍、社会动荡的战国时期；面对乱世的苦难与个体的困境，他没有像儒墨那样积极救世，而是转向了对个体精神自由的追求，开创了一种超脱乱世、安顿心灵的智慧。庄子继承并发展了老子开创的道家思想，与老子并称\"老庄\"。本章揭示庄子思想的时代根源与道家渊源。\n"}